id: pm-presets-ci-v2
title: Apply Fleet CI v2 quick PR and deep validation tiers
description: "Companion pm-cli-website-dyhg. Preserve required checks while moving exhaustive validation to deep CI, use deterministic quick seeded prefixes, retain unchanged coverage thresholds and Windows platform contracts."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: ci,"gh:unbraind/pm-presets#225",performance
created_at: "2026-11-15T12:07:59.050Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-15T14:33:13.844Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-15T12:08:01.577Z",codex-sol,"Oriented with context, CI/flaky searches and open items; no matching active CI tier task exists. Pilot pm-csv PR #258 reviewed. Required checks: test (22), test (26), windows-prepare-lifecycle. CodeQL is optional. Retain Windows parser/lifecycle contracts in quick CI and move duplicate simulation release gates into the full npm/Bun deep matrix. Release workflows and verifier scripts remain outside scope."
  "2026-11-15T12:11:29.073Z",codex-sol,"Latest successful main CI run 43679647905: created-to-completed test (22) 32m37s, test (26) 27m50s, simulation gates 27m37s, Windows 2m32s. Logs retrieved through the run archive because gh run view --log returned empty. Slowest full-depth packed test 154.33s, stack model 28.93s, parameter model 15.29s. Wave-1 PR #221 has one successful CI run and no failures. Quick prefixes cover seven property corpora without threshold changes; operational packed/lock/admission watchdogs scale by PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE. Packed acceptance runs artifacts under Bun but does not prove Bun package-manager/bunx installation; explicit graph-install and pinned bunx CLI smoke added."
  "2026-11-15T12:12:05.176Z",codex-sol,"Implemented quick/deep workflows and tier inventory. Typecheck, lint, build, test compilation and four CI/depth/watchdog contract tests passed (linked command 3.66s). Strict YAML parsing passed for all three workflows, with explicit timeouts on every job; actionlint is unavailable. Targeted quick tests are running. Push early for authoritative hosted CI feedback; local quick coverage will be bounded to 20 minutes. No full-depth suite is run locally."
  "2026-11-15T12:14:35.138Z",codex-sol,"PR #225 opened at head e8628b9. CI run 43712692286 and CodeQL run 43712692186 are queued. Six real git-diff classifier scenarios passed (docs, tracker data, executable tracker, newline filenames, LICENSE and source-to-docs rename); pinned bunx host smoke returned 2026.11.10. Strict health passes with fresh user state, matching CI; the initial local mismatch came from a user-scoped extension rather than repository configuration, so no dependency change is needed."
  "2026-11-15T12:20:32.215Z",codex-sol,"Touched quick test command passed 73/73 tests with zero failures, skips or cancellations in 8m24.12s (Node 24 on a contended shared host). The four CI/depth/watchdog tests passed separately. One PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick npm run coverage run has now started on Node 26, bounded to 1200 seconds. No full-depth run was started. Hosted required jobs remain queued at the latest observation."
  "2026-11-15T12:31:12.285Z",codex-sol,"The single quick coverage run completed in 9m43.05s on Node 26: 370 tests, 367 passed, three failed, zero skips/cancellations; the unchanged source scope reported 100% lines/branches/functions. Failures were fixture routing, not missing coverage or timing: linked-test schema context supplies PM_PATH, and two audited-settings tests plus the all-presets SDK child CLI inherited it instead of their disposable tracker. Make child roots explicit, then rerun only the two affected files in the same linked-test context. No second local coverage run will be performed; hosted CI must certify the final complete suite."
  "2026-11-15T12:32:50.222Z",codex-sol,"Fixture fixes passed 9/9 with zero skips/cancellations in 20.63s under the same linked-test schema context. Final typecheck, lint and test compilation passed in 2.99s. Independent LCOV verification matched exactly all 36 configured sources: 6645/6645 lines, 1972/1972 branches and 388/388 functions hit. The complete coverage command remains recorded as failed (367/370 before the root-isolation fix); no second coverage run. Final hosted quick CI and post-merge full depth remain required evidence. Original PR CI run 43712692286 is still queued after approximately 20 minutes; no completed wall time can be reported. Release the claim at handoff and leave the item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-15T13:42:47.591Z",codex-sol,"Review round: preserve cheap-path privacy and identity checks where applicable, restore portable test behavior, and verify generated-case assertions. Run targeted gates and required revert proofs; leave review threads untouched and wait for the dispatch hold before pushing."
  "2026-11-15T13:48:55.891Z",codex-sol,"Review finding PRRT_kwDOSp_1PM63pVlR fixed: generated success/refusal counters start at zero, independent of setup cases, and thresholds use the generated-case budget. Linked gates passed: typecheck, build, test compilation, lint, 32 artifact/workflow/tooling tests, strict unique-key YAML and changelog. Revert proof at quick depth: omitting both generated outcome increments fails with zero-based counters, but passes after reverting to seeded 2/1 counters. A separate omitted-refusal control fails the refusal assertion. Scratch copies removed. No measured coverage sources changed; package coverage was not run."
  "2026-11-15T14:24:11.576Z",codex-sol,"Round 2: fixing the supplied review findings, auditing the whole CI v2 diff for the same defect classes, and running the requested focused gates. Review threads remain untouched."
  "2026-11-15T14:32:27.898Z",codex-sol,"Round 2: validate both scale-derived budgets before any fixture state or spawn; pass the validated worker budget as an argument, clear watchdogs on spawn errors, and enforce worker-local deadlines in both synchronous and asynchronous polling loops. A thrown filesystem-hook timeout can be caught by product cleanup, so expiry terminates the fixture worker explicitly. Invalid-scale/no-spawn and both independent-deadline regressions now pass. Audited every remaining testTime call: spawnSync option evaluation precedes launch; barrier waits are bounded and enclosed in cleanup."
  "2026-11-15T14:33:11.634Z",codex-sol,"Validation passed: typecheck, lint, build:test and 27 touched-lock/workflow/tooling tests via pm test --run --only-last --progress; both worker self-expiry paths and scale-zero/no-spawn are included. Every workflow passed strict unique-key YAML parsing. No item is closed; release the claim for orchestrator verification."
